<aside><h1>Web Based Parking</h1><p>Responsive Folio3 Parking web app. Employees sign in with Google and are routed by their verified role to the employee or administrator workspace. Employees see their assignment, register a vehicle if needed, release or schedule a dedicated space, and eligible employees claim released spaces. Parking Administrators manage employee assignments, parking settings and roles, inspect weekly utilization and entry checks, and review retained audit history. Authentication validation, email delivery, weekly job execution, and trusted LPR/hardware commands are backend integrations, not separate user pages. All pages use the light visual treatment, shared role-specific header, consistent sample records, and responsive phone, tablet, and desktop layouts.</p><h3>Screens</h3><ul><li><a href="#S-1">S-1 <code>/sign-in</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-2">S-2 <code>/parking</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-3">S-3 <code>/parking/release</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-4">S-4 <code>/parking/schedule</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-5">S-5 <code>/parking/available</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-6">S-6 <code>/account/vehicles</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-7">S-7 <code>/admin</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-8">S-8 <code>/admin/employees</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-9">S-9 <code>/admin/employees/:employeeId</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-10">S-10 <code>/admin/parking-setup</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-11">S-11 <code>/admin/reports/weekly</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-12">S-12 <code>/admin/entry-checks</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-13">S-13 <code>/admin/audit</code></a></li></ul><h3>No screen</h3><ul><li><b>REQ-14</b> When a released parking allocation becomes claimable, the Folio3 Parking web app shall send an email notification using a fixed template to eligible employees without dedicated parking who have a registered vehicle. <i>(no screen: Claimable-space email delivery is a fixed-template background notification to eligible employees with a registered vehicle and no dedicated space. There is no separate email-settings or notification page required; the resulting availability is shown on S-5.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-15</b> If a permanently stickered vehicle arrives, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall leave its existing sticker process unaffected and preserve any temporary claim already made for that date, including when configured capacity is exceeded. <i>(no screen: Keeping the existing permanent vehicle-sticker process unaffected and preserving a temporary claim when capacity is exceeded is integration behavior, not a user-facing page or control.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-16</b> When the Folio3 LPR integration submits an entrance-verification request, the Folio3 Parking web app shall authenticate the request as originating from trusted Folio3 LPR equipment, require a unique authenticated request ID or nonce and reject any previously accepted ID or nonce, then verify a detected car&#39;s readable plate against that date&#39;s temporary parking authorizations and activate the green indicator only for a valid authorization. <i>(no screen: Trusted Folio3 LPR equipment authentication, unique authenticated request IDs/nonces, replay rejection, plate authorization and green-indicator activation are entrance integration and hardware behavior. S-12 displays recorded outcomes but is not an LPR control page.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-17</b> If any entrance verification fails, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall issue an explicit command to set the green indicator inactive and deny entry through the temporary-parking process. <i>(no screen: Explicitly deactivating the green indicator and denying temporary-process entry on verification failure is a fail-safe integration command, not a user-facing page. S-12 displays the resulting denial and indicator outcome.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-21</b> Where a Parking Administrator has configured a named report-recipient list, the Folio3 Parking web app shall send weekly employee-identifying report emails only to configured recipients who have the Parking Administrator role, omitting all other listed addresses from delivery. <i>(no screen: The actual Monday email job and filtering delivery to configured recipients with the Parking Administrator role are background behavior. S-10 provides the named recipient configuration and role visibility; there is no separate email-delivery page.)</i></li></ul></aside>
